From 693442c04a4834d03cd5fac95fb8e06633448acb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 15:08:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Redecorate: six house styles, and a site finder for five more
 portals

Which template level is which OSRS house style was never established. The
template maps answer it: each of the six levels builds its rooms out of a
different wall set AND carries its own complete dungeon set, and the materials
run wood, stone, whitewashed stone, Fremennik, tropical, fancy stone - exactly
the OSRS ladder. So the names, levels and prices are OSRS's own.

The estate agent's second option is real now: he names your current style,
offers the six over two chat pages, checks the level, takes the coins and
writes %poh_style. Nothing rebuilds - he stands outside the portal, and the
furniture is stored per hotspot, which is why this is decoration and not
demolition. The purse is re-checked after the confirm box, which is a suspend.

Relocate stops at the one question a checker cannot answer. It needs a
five-tile portal standing in five more towns, and siting the FIRST one cost
five shipped placements because a 377 loc sits at one height with the ground
running through it. tools/portalsite.py does the computable part - level
ground, nothing solid, off the dirt road, beside the town's own path - and
::~pohtown <0-5> puts you on each candidate so ::~pohportal can show you one.

The tool validates on Rimmington: excluding the tile the portal occupies, its
best answer is one tile from the 7,23 that took five attempts by hand.

rs2check 0 ERROR / 0 CHECK; poh_battery ALL PASS (53 groups);
poh_mutate 53/53 caught.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J1qUhTcu63bJ3hCBBxy7nU
